From: macos15-guest-stack <kirin@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drain: log the head of a payload-carrying CmdNOP

CmdNOP is documented as a fence carrying stamps and no payload, and the
drain retires its header stamps while dropping the bytes.  On the
2026-09-17 stalled boot the guest sent it with 124/172/196-byte payloads
on channel 1, so "no payload" is a description the guest does not always
keep, and dropping the bytes is only the whole contract if they carry
nothing the guest waits on.

NopCarriedPayload now carries the first 16 bytes of the dropped payload,
hex-encoded, so the next boot can classify the command form this arm does
not decode instead of only counting it.

Apply on top of 0002 in the reims-vgpu source root:  patch -p1 < this file

diff --git a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/drain/mod.rs b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/drain/mod.rs
index 58da9538..659e94af 100644
--- a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/drain/mod.rs
+++ b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/drain/mod.rs
@@ -153,6 +153,14 @@ fn release_translation_order_holds(state: &mut DeviceState) {
 pub(crate) struct NopCarriedPayload {
     pub(crate) channel: u32,
     pub(crate) plen: usize,
+    /// First bytes of the dropped payload, hex-encoded, so a boot can classify
+    /// the command form this arm does not decode. CmdNOP is documented as "a
+    /// fence carrying stamps and no payload"; the guest on the 2026-09-17
+    /// stalled boot sent it with 124/172/196-byte payloads on channel 1, and
+    /// retiring the header stamps while dropping the bytes is only the whole
+    /// contract if the payload carries nothing the guest waits on. The head is
+    /// what answers that question next time.
+    pub(crate) head_hex: String,
 }
 
 impl crate::observe::Decline for NopCarriedPayload {
@@ -164,6 +180,7 @@ impl crate::observe::Decline for NopCarriedPayload {
         vec![
             ("ch", self.channel.to_string()),
             ("plen", self.plen.to_string()),
+            ("head", self.head_hex.clone()),
         ]
     }
 }
@@ -6651,6 +6674,12 @@ fn process_child_packet<H: HostMemory + HostOps>(
                     &NopCarriedPayload {
                         channel: channel_id,
                         plen: packet.payload.len(),
+                        head_hex: packet
+                            .payload
+                            .iter()
+                            .take(16)
+                            .map(|b| format!("{b:02x}"))
+                            .collect(),
                     },
                 )
                 .fail();
